<article class="env-example" id="0BMW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BMW">Example <span data-tag="0BMW">58.3.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category and let $F : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ be a functor such that $F(X)$ is finite for all $X \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0BMR" data-tag="0BMR">58.3.1</a> we see that $G = \text{Aut}(F)$ comes endowed with the structure of a profinite topological group in a canonical manner. We obtain a functor </p>
  <div class="equation" id="0BMX">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/0BMX" data-tag="0BMX">58.3.5.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{pione-equation-remember} \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \textit{Finite-}G\textit{-Sets},\quad X \longmapsto F(X) \end{equation}</div>
</div>
  <p> where $F(X)$ is endowed with the induced action of $G$. This action is continuous by our construction of the topology on $\text{Aut}(F)$. </p>
</article>